// Rule 3: a borrowed name may not also be a variable. `fmod` is an ordinary
// identifier in every file that does not borrow it; in one that does, the
// name is spoken for, and `real fmod` beside a call to `fmod` would be one
// name meaning two things in one file - the hazard the language already
// named when it refused `pi : 3`.
//
// Stricter than a constant, which may be had by declaring it. There is no
// declaring your way out of a borrow: the clause has claimed the name for
// the whole file, so the cure is at one line or the other, and the message
// names both.
uses fmod

fun <> = main() {
  real fmod : 2.5
  ? fmod
}
